# Dropdowns Must Be Searchable

Always use the shared `SearchableSelect` component for dropdowns/selects so
users can filter options by typing. Do not introduce plain `<select>` elements
or non-searchable Radix `Select` usages for option lists.

Import from `@/components/ui/searchable-select`.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — searchable by default
import { SearchableSelect } from "@/components/ui/searchable-select";

<SearchableSelect
  options={options}            // { value, label, description?, keywords? }[]
  value={value}
  onValueChange={onChange}
  placeholder="Select an option"
  searchPlaceholder="Search…"
/>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — not searchable
<select value={value} onChange={onChange}>
  {options.map((o) => <option key={o.value} value={o.value}>{o.label}</option>)}
</select>
```

Notes:
- `SearchableSelect` is searchable by default (`searchable` prop defaults to `true`). Only set `searchable={false}` when there is a clear, explicit reason.
- For remote/server-side search use `manualFiltering`, `onSearchChange`, and `loading`.
- Use `keywords` on options to improve matching (search is accent-insensitive).
